"""
RoManager - Roblox multi-account manager and multi-instance launcher (single file).
Python 3.11+, Windows 10/11 x64.  Dependencies: customtkinter, psutil, Pillow, pywebview.

Multi-instance works by creating and holding the singleton guard objects that Roblox
checks before it opens a new client.  Clients that were already open before RoManager
took the guard must be closed once; after that there is no instance-count limit except
what your PC can handle.  RoManager never opens, duplicates or closes handles inside
another process.

Roblox clients open inside RoManager's Multi-View tiles by default, so the desktop stays
clean.  The tile under the pointer runs at full speed; every other client keeps running
in the background with reduced priority and Efficiency Mode.

Not implemented (no fake buttons): tray icon, language packs, auto-updater,
whole-file database encryption (secrets are DPAPI-encrypted per field), adopting
Roblox clients that were started before RoManager.

Build as an exe with:
  pyinstaller --onedir --windowed --name RoManager --collect-all customtkinter --collect-all webview romanager.py
(--onefile also works, but every login window then re-extracts the exe and starts slower.)
Debug build (shows a console with errors): same command with --console instead of --windowed.

Start-up guarantees in this version:
  * The main window is never hidden with withdraw(). It is transparent while it is built, then it is made visible
    and a loop verifies that Windows really shows it (re-showing it, and moving it on-screen, if not).
  * A second launch finds the running window by Tk class + title (not by title alone), shows it even if it was
    hidden, and if the running copy has no window at all it offers to end that stale copy and start fresh.
  * Nothing slow runs before the window exists: the multi-instance mutex is set up in a background thread, and
    RoManager's own CPU ceiling / efficiency mode start only a few seconds after the window is visible.
  * "Start minimized" only applies when Windows autostarts RoManager (--autostart). Double-click always shows it.
  * startup.log (in %APPDATA%\\RoManager) records every start-up step; a watchdog writes thread stacks to crash.log
    and shows a message box if the window is not visible within 45 seconds.

Lifecycle guarantees in this version:
  * Closing the window ends RoManager completely: worker threads stop, the login window process tree is killed,
    the CPU / RAM / efficiency / affinity limits RoManager put on your Roblox clients are taken back, job-object
    handles and the multi-instance objects are released, the database is closed, and the process exits
    (with a hard-exit watchdog in case anything hangs).
  * The login window process always ends with os._exit: when login finishes, when its window is closed,
    when RoManager is gone, or after 30 minutes. It is also placed in a kill-on-close job object.
  * Startup errors and crashes in a windowed exe are shown in a message box and written to crash.log,
    and the process still exits cleanly afterwards.
  * Logs, history tables and temp files are bounded, and per-client job handles are closed when a client exits.
"""
import collections, ctypes, hashlib, hmac, io, json, math, os, queue, random
import re, secrets, shutil, sqlite3, subprocess, sys, threading, time, urllib.error
import urllib.parse, urllib.request
from ctypes import wintypes
from datetime import datetime
from pathlib import Path
from tkinter import colorchooser, messagebox

# A windowed PyInstaller build (no console) gives this process sys.stdout / sys.stderr = None.
# Any print() would then raise before a window appears. Redirect them up front.
if getattr(sys, "frozen", False):
    if sys.stdout is None:
        sys.stdout = open(os.devnull, "w")
    if sys.stderr is None:
        sys.stderr = open(os.devnull, "w")

if sys.platform != "win32":
    print("RoManager only runs on Windows 10/11.")
    sys.exit(1)


def _fatal(msg):
    try:
        ctypes.windll.user32.MessageBoxW(0, msg, "RoManager", 0x10)
    except Exception:
        pass
    os._exit(1)


try:
    import psutil
    import customtkinter as ctk
except Exception:
    import traceback
    _fatal("RoManager could not start because a required component is missing:\n\n"
           + traceback.format_exc()[-900:])

try:
    from PIL import Image
except Exception:  # avatars are optional
    Image = None

APP_NAME = "RoManager"
APPDIR = Path(os.environ.get("APPDATA", ".")) / APP_NAME
PROC_NAME = "RobloxPlayerBeta.exe"
NCPU = psutil.cpu_count() or 1
MAX_ACCOUNTS = 40  # supported ceiling for the account list, imports and launch queue
READY = threading.Event()  # set once the main window has been verified visible


